@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Implements JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Returns the value `pointer` refers to in `document` (the empty pointer
+returns the whole document). Throws `JsonPointerError` if the pointer is malformed (sections 3 and 6: must be
+empty or start with `/`, `~` only as `~0`/`~1`) or does not resolve (section 4: missing member, array index
+out of range or not canonical, `-`, or descending into a primitive/`null`). A member whose value is `null`
+resolves to `null`. Only own properties are followed; the document is never modified.
